# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database — Postgres, via Prisma. TWO URLs (see prisma/schema.prisma):
#   DATABASE_URL  — runtime queries. On serverless this MUST be a pooler.
#   DIRECT_URL    — `prisma db push` / `prisma migrate` only (a real session).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CMP-4: production URLs MUST carry TLS — Prisma reads SSL from the query
# string, and src/lib/db.ts warns in production if `sslmode` is absent.
#
# ── Supabase + Vercel (or any serverless host) ──────────────────────────
# The direct host `db.<ref>.supabase.co` is IPv6-only. Vercel functions
# have no IPv6 egress, so a direct URL there fails EVERY query
# (/api/health/ready → {"database":"error"}). Use the connection pooler
# (Supavisor), which is IPv4. Copy both strings from the Supabase
# dashboard → Project Settings → Database → Connection string:
#
#   DATABASE_URL = "Transaction pooler"  — host aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com,
#                  port 6543, user postgres.<ref>. Append pgbouncer + a small pool:
#   DIRECT_URL   = "Session pooler" (port 5432 on the same pooler host) or the
#                  direct connection if your migration runner has IPv4 to it.
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<ref>:PASSWORD@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1&sslmode=require"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.<ref>:PASSWORD@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"
#
# ── Generic managed Postgres (Neon / RDS) ──────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@POOLER_HOST:PORT/DBNAME?schema=public&sslmode=require"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@DIRECT_HOST:5432/DBNAME?schema=public&sslmode=require"
#
# ── Local dev against a plain local server (no TLS) ─────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/a2r_dos?schema=public"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/a2r_dos?schema=public"
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@POOLER_HOST:PORT/DBNAME?schema=public&sslmode=require"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@DIRECT_HOST:5432/DBNAME?schema=public&sslmode=require"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Preview / Production data-isolation guardrail (P0 #4)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The build AND the runtime hard-fail if a Vercel Preview / Development
# deployment (VERCEL_ENV = preview | development) is wired to the PRODUCTION
# database. Local `next dev` and CI are never gated (no VERCEL_* vars).
# See docs/PREVIEW_ENVIRONMENT_ISOLATION.md for the full Vercel setup.
#
# The production Supabase project ref is baked into the code as a default,
# so nothing is required here. Set these only if the production database is
# migrated to a new project/host:
# PRODUCTION_SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF="xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"   # the <ref> in db.<ref>.supabase.co
# PRODUCTION_DB_HOST="db.example.supabase.co"              # alternative / additional match
#
# DELIBERATE local-only override — permits a non-production build to use the
# production DB. NEVER set this on a shared Vercel environment.
# ALLOW_PROD_DB_OUTSIDE_PROD=true

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NextAuth
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# Use a DIFFERENT secret for Preview vs Production (Vercel env-var scoping)
# so a session minted in one environment can't be replayed against the other.
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="CHANGE_ME"
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Front door — site routing mode (server-only; src/middleware.ts)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Strict enum. NOT a NEXT_PUBLIC_ var — the routing decision never reaches
# the browser or the build artifact. Fail-closed: a missing / misspelled /
# unknown value is treated as `marketing`, NEVER as "show the app". A Vercel
# *production* build with no valid value fails outright (next.config.mjs).
#
#   marketing  — `/` serves the public early-access page (cacheable). DEFAULT.
#   internal   — `/` forwards anonymous visitors to /launch (full app as the
#                front door — internal / preview deployments).
#   live       — `/` forwards anonymous visitors to /login (product launched).
#
# A signed-in visitor is always forwarded to /launch regardless of mode.
# See docs/SITE_ROUTING_MODEL.md.
A2R_SITE_MODE="marketing"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data retention (CMP-2)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Days to keep high-volume ephemeral records before the retention sweep
# (src/server/services/data-retention.ts) deletes them. Omit any line to
# use the default shown. The immutable compliance ledger is NEVER swept.
# RETENTION_ACTIVITY_LOG_DAYS=730          # 24 months  — PS Control Tower activity feed
# RETENTION_AUDIT_LOG_DAYS=2555            # ~7 years   — governance audit trail
# RETENTION_IMPERSONATION_GRANT_DAYS=545   # 18 months  — ended / long-expired grants
# RETENTION_API_KEY_DAYS=365               # 12 months  — revoked / long-expired keys

# Shared secret for POST /api/internal/retention so a cron scheduler can
# trigger the sweep (header: x-a2r-internal-token). Unset = the endpoint
# only accepts an authenticated A2R staff session.
# RETENTION_API_TOKEN="CHANGE_ME"
